Make quill 11.1.0 build under Bazel 9.

Bazel 9 removed the implicit availability of native `cc_library` (and
sibling cc_* rules) in BUILD files. Quill's BCR-shipped BUILD.bazel
relies on the implicit symbol, so loading must be made explicit.

Upstream tracking: this can be dropped once quill (or its BCR entry)
publishes a release whose BUILD.bazel has the load() statement.

--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+load("@rules_cc//cc:defs.bzl", "cc_library")
+
 package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])
 
 licenses(["notice"])  # MIT
